      "message": "fix(session): reset empty-turn content without removing its message identity (#2695)\n\n* fix(session): reset empty-turn content without removing its message identity\n\nDropping a think-only/empty step used to delete the assistant message and\nrebuild it under the same ID for the retry. On the wire that sequence is\nidentical to a late frame of an already-deleted entity, so consumers that\norder by events discard the retried content permanently and the whole reply\ndisappears from the UI until the engine restarts.\n\nReset the parts instead, matching what the retry cleanup already does with\nremovePart: the message identity survives, retried content lands on it, and\nno deletion fact is published.\n\nRefs docs/compose/spec/empty-turn-part-reset.md\n\n* docs(session): finalize empty-turn spec and apply review follow-ups\n\nCorrect the stale drop-path comment so it describes resetting parts rather\nthan deleting and rebuilding the message, release the regression test's bus\nsubscription with ensuring so a throwing prompt cannot leak it, and record\nthe verification evidence plus the corrected exhaustion behaviour in the\nfeature document.\n\n* docs(session): point empty-turn spec at PR #2695\n\n* docs(session): make empty-turn spec English-only and link its PR",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "09c75767d15f3ffae0e10370f3d84866eb022247",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/XiaomiMiMo/MiMo-Code/git/trees/09c75767d15f3ffae0e10370f3d84866eb022247"
      },
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/XiaomiMiMo/MiMo-Code/git/commits/a7440d13b2aa55d435a03d1ff36d1e7a4f7abc8e",
      "comment_count": 0,
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJq2G2bCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQKkQAIiFdjyzkXzFtrM7/NG7wtqu\nPBeORjGAeU8w/7pvIaJ8VNfgIdxHH3TdJI2j8vGsKvmgPgdADfgMBRl2VUdP9ahh\n5p/5m8Gs/BprMGDXJp+c2tZ5P5VEF1rVhu3XRhbFMr06pjytvZD3AJN0kVx7z3EC\niPo8GUkR2yyl8WSwidVPntLNn9Kx+mooKelr9CSvBY39bACZEdDXfkUos8QefbST\nFP0wJS2lgD9F8qljIT6IgtjioSgjJ0CDuVi4C/6nhMacrebqJPoQDcGUx2J85uCv\nSphn7WqWEPfZmie2vQLGfnt0lYpTPQEKxc3WGY+Ltzsdw1nIcgHltO89qlNLOt97\nW3WBsWHUQ8WZLw61vLaEpVHjjSLaR5mVYjfb079l723Zduwu38vDfJ2zZmXX3fJO\nUxL39QY7B3/ueYCwjjyyYyFLdTGyv7HbidzfEdSpQEO+c69NZT0imJwYKGVp/sMO\n7BjhiZcl08NM2kDkmMJqHb76JWd7CYxrOSyCKrj/zNEltFlaSf5MYUPGcbaMOKQo\nlguUluKsU+dLujJ+hpN73zcuQRpMOVDmzFF0ewSaFhnnQWgwpOu9YfDRbLmWuqlJ\nKN1w5uIQEkGfJAU/4IMNmPFCcqJGubMow4wvIOzLT2uWcZSYDJoT5jQcDzg+BKh5\nyepfudXO1MuK85KKQZfd\n=Oaql\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n",
        "payload": "tree 09c75767d15f3ffae0e10370f3d84866eb022247\nparent 12a59e9013734948c1a6b557fe45db2e9f417286\nauthor Yihan Yan <yanyihan@xiaomi.com> 1792568731 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1792568731 +0800\n\nfix(session): reset empty-turn content without removing its message identity (#2695)\n\n* fix(session): reset empty-turn content without removing its message identity\n\nDropping a think-only/empty step used to delete the assistant message and\nrebuild it under the same ID for the retry. On the wire that sequence is\nidentical to a late frame of an already-deleted entity, so consumers that\norder by events discard the retried content permanently and the whole reply\ndisappears from the UI until the engine restarts.\n\nReset the parts instead, matching what the retry cleanup already does with\nremovePart: the message identity survives, retried content lands on it, and\nno deletion fact is published.\n\nRefs docs/compose/spec/empty-turn-part-reset.md\n\n* docs(session): finalize empty-turn spec and apply review follow-ups\n\nCorrect the stale drop-path comment so it describes resetting parts rather\nthan deleting and rebuilding the message, release the regression test's bus\nsubscription with ensuring so a throwing prompt cannot leak it, and record\nthe verification evidence plus the corrected exhaustion behaviour in the\nfeature document.\n\n* docs(session): point empty-turn spec at PR #2695\n\n* docs(session): make empty-turn spec English-only and link its PR",
        "verified_at": "2026-10-21T07:45:31Z"
      }
